SUMMARY: Toronto Country Fest: Callie McCullough
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by timeless classics\, modern singer/songwriter Call
 ie McCullough has followed her unique muse for years. Her debut album Aft
 er Midnight featured contributions from Grammy-winning bluegrass band Uni
 on Station and western-swing supergroup The Time Jumpers. Her Sophomore r
 elease Cutting Through The Noise – is a bold\, bright reimagining of Nort
 h American roots music as diverse and defiant as the songwriter who made 
 it. Rich with ethereal soundscapes and earthy\, organic arrangements-it’s
  a gorgeous blend of Celtic\, folk\, traditional country\, Appalachian bl
 uegrass\, and atmospheric Americana\, all tied together by a woman whose 
 voice has earned comparisons to Dolly Parton and Alison Krauss.
