SUMMARY: Parade: Queer Acts of Love & Resistance
DESCRIPTION:The queer resistance that changed Canada—and the rights we ca
 n’t take for granted.\n\nA new monthly series in partnership with Hot Doc
 s\, bringing visionary documentary filmmaking from around the world to To
 ronto’s East End.\n\nParade: Queer Acts of Love & Resistance captures a w
 ide range of pivotal moments that sparked Canada’s 2SLGBTQI+ movement and
  its progress\, and honours the activists and elders whose resistance led
  to the rights we have today. Rarely seen archival footage and first-pers
 on accounts bring the viewer to the frontlines of the decades-long strugg
 le.\n\nFrom police raids to early drag shows\, community organizing to ad
 dresses to the House of Commons—the complex history of the country’s dive
 rse communities is brought to life. Key milestones illustrate the power o
 f taking resistance into the streets and underscore how easily the rights
  we’ve fought for can be revoked\, making this essential viewing for all 
 Canadians. Unflinching\, bold\, enraging\, hopeful: Parade is a vital new
  chapter in the queer film canon.\n\nMore information can be found here: 
 https://soulpepper.ca/parade-queer-acts-of-love-resistance/ https://soulp
 epper.ca/parade-queer-acts-of-love-resistance/ .
CATEGORIES:free,movie,documentary,queer
