SUMMARY: Toronto Star Live at Soulpepper: Chrystia Freeland on Power\, De
 mocracy and a Changing World
DESCRIPTION:How should Canada respond when the old rules no longer apply?
 \n\nAcclaimed journalist and former deputy prime minister Chrystia Freela
 nd joins Star business columnist Adam Radwanski for the launch of Toronto
  Star Live at Soulpepper — a conversation about what Canada and other dem
 ocracies owe each other\, and themselves\, when the old rules no longer a
 pply. How should Canada respond when powerful countries — including its c
 losest neighbours — become unpredictable partners?\n\nHer new book\, Unre
 liable Boyfriend: An Insider’s View of Dealing with a Chaotic Superpower\
 , Plutocrats and Other Complicated People\, is a firsthand account of tha
 t pressure — and an argument for what comes next.\n\nMore information and
  tickets can be found here: https://soulpepper.ca/toronto-star-live-in-co
 nversation-with-chrystia-freeland/ https://soulpepper.ca/toronto-star-liv
 e-in-conversation-with-chrystia-freeland/ .
CATEGORIES:toronto-star,live-journalism,talk
